            "logprobs": [],
            "text": "For a **hotel-led mixed-use project with private branded residences**, the following brands are commonly included in an initial global long list. The appropriate shortlist depends heavily on location, buyer profile, hotel size, pricing, and the developer’s economics.\n\n## 1. Core ultra-luxury brands\n\nThese are usually considered first for prime gateway-city, resort, and trophy projects:\n\n- **Four Seasons Private Residences**\n- **The Ritz-Carlton Residences**\n- **St. Regis Residences**\n- **Mandarin Oriental Residences**\n- **Rosewood Residences**\n- **Waldorf Astoria Residences**\n- **Raffles Residences**\n- **Aman Residences**\n- **One&Only Private Homes**\n- **Park Hyatt Residences**\n\nThese brands generally offer the strongest combination of global recognition, high-touch residential management, luxury buyer appeal, and experience with shared hotel-residence operations. Four Seasons, for example, has operated branded real estate since 1985, while Marriott has built a broad residential platform around Ritz-Carlton, St. Regis and its other brands. ([press.fourseasons.com](https://press.fourseasons.com/news-releases/2024/private-residences-growth/?utm_source=openai))\n\n## 2. Luxury resort, wellness and classic hospitality brands\n\nOften considered for beachfront, mountain, golf, wellness and destination-resort developments:\n\n- **Six Senses Residences**\n- **Banyan Tree Residences**\n- **Fairmont Residences**\n- **Regent Residences**\n- **Conrad Residences**\n- **LXR Residences**\n- **Alila Residences**\n- **Kempinski Residences**\n- **Ritz-Carlton Reserve Residences**\n- **JW Marriott Residences**\n- **The Luxury Collection Residences**\n- **Montage Residences**\n- **Auberge Collection residences**\n\nSix Senses, Regent, InterContinental and Kimpton form IHG’s principal residential brand platform, while Banyan Group offers residences through Banyan Tree, Angsana and other brands. ([ihg.com](https://www.ihg.com/residences/content/us/en/brands?utm_source=openai))\n\n## 3. Luxury lifestyle and design-led brands\n\nThese can be a better fit where the buyer proposition is driven by design, entertainment, food and beverage, nightlife or a younger ownership demographic:\n\n- **W Residences**\n- **EDITION Residences**\n- **SLS Residences**\n- **Delano Residences**\n- **Mondrian Residences**\n- **SO/ Residences**\n- **Andaz Residences**\n- **Thompson Hotels Residences**\n- **The Standard Residences**\n- **Kimpton Residences**\n- **Pendry Residences**\n- **Faena Residences**\n- **Hyde Residences**\n- **25hours Residences**\n- **Mama Shelter Residences**\n\nMarriott currently promotes a multi-brand residential platform including W and EDITION, Hyatt is expanding residences under Andaz, Thompson and The Standard, and Accor’s portfolio includes SLS, Delano, Mondrian, SO/, Hyde and other lifestyle brands. ([marriottresidences.com](https://marriottresidences.com/brands/?utm_source=openai))\n\n## 4. Broader luxury and upper-upscale brands\n\nFor projects requiring a more accessible residential price point or larger number of units, developers may also evaluate:\n\n### Marriott\n- Marriott Residences\n- Westin Residences\n- Sheraton Residences\n- Le Méridien Residences\n- Renaissance Residences\n- Autograph Collection Residences\n- Tribute Portfolio Residences\n- Apartments by Marriott Bonvoy\n\nMarriott has one of the broadest platforms, with approximately 16–17 residential brands spanning luxury through premium positioning. ([marriottresidences.com](https://marriottresidences.com/brands/?utm_source=openai))\n\n### Hilton\n- Hilton Residences\n- Curio Collection by Hilton residences\n- Canopy by Hilton residences\n- Signia by Hilton residences\n- DoubleTree by Hilton residences\n- Embassy Suites residences\n\nHilton’s residential portfolio spans nine brands and includes both hotel/resort residences and private-residence structures. ([hilton.com](https://www.hilton.com/en/corporate/residential-development/?utm_source=openai))\n\n### Accor\n- Sofitel Residences\n- MGallery Residences\n- Pullman Residences\n- Swissôtel Residences\n- Mövenpick Residences\n- Rixos Residences\n- Fairmont Residences\n\nAccor says its residential platform covers more than 25 hospitality brands, ranging from midscale to ultra-luxury. ([group.accor.com](https://group.accor.com/en/hotel-development/solutions-for-every-project?mdrv=group.accor.com&utm_source=openai))\n\n### Hyatt and IHG\n- Grand Hyatt Residences\n- Hyatt Regency residences\n- InterContinental Residences\n- Kimpton Residences\n\nHyatt reports more than 50 residential projects open or in its pipeline across brands such as Park Hyatt, Andaz, Thompson and The Standard. IHG’s established residential offering is concentrated around Six Senses, Regent, InterContinental and Kimpton. ([newsroom.hyatt.com](https://newsroom.hyatt.com/may-30-2025-unscriptedbyhyatt?utm_source=openai))\n\n## Practical first-round shortlist\n\nFor a typical international feasibility or operator-selection exercise, I would usually start with:\n\n### Prime urban luxury\n1. Four Seasons  \n2. Ritz-Carlton  \n3. St. Regis  \n4. Mandarin Oriental  \n5. Rosewood  \n6. Waldorf Astoria  \n7. Raffles  \n8. Park Hyatt  \n\n### Ultra-luxury resort\n1. Four Seasons  \n2. One&Only  \n3. Aman  \n4. Rosewood  \n5. Ritz-Carlton Reserve  \n6. Six Senses  \n7. Mandarin Oriental  \n8. Banyan Tree  \n\n### Luxury lifestyle\n1. W  \n2. EDITION  \n3. SLS  \n4. Andaz  \n5. Thompson  \n6. The Standard  \n7. Mondrian  \n8. Kimpton or Pendry  \n\n### Upper-luxury or premium mixed-use\n1. JW Marriott  \n2. Fairmont  \n3. Conrad  \n4. InterContinental  \n5. Marriott  \n6. Westin  \n7. Sofitel  \n8. Grand Hyatt  \n\n## The brand should ultimately be selected on more than prestige\n\nThe operator comparison should examine:\n\n- **Brand recognition among the project’s likely buyers**\n- **Achievable residential sales premium and absorption**\n- **Hotel positioning and achievable room rate**\n- **Experience managing homeowners’ associations**\n- **Residential service-charge levels**\n- **Rental-program capability**\n- **Hotel and residence amenity-sharing arrangements**\n- **Brand and management fees**\n- **Territorial availability and competing-area restrictions**\n- **Technical-services and design requirements**\n- **Minimum hotel keys and maximum residence-to-hotel ratio**\n- **Developer guarantees, key money or working-capital requirements**\n- **Brand strength in the buyers’ source markets**\n\nA key distinction is that a **branded residence is normally a privately owned home licensed and serviced under a hospitality brand**. It is not the same as an extended-stay hotel or serviced-apartment brand—so, for example, *Residence Inn* should not automatically be treated as a branded residential ownership product."
